{"schema_version":3,"seq":53,"ts":"2026-11-08T19:46:06Z","type":"finding_annotated","finding":"F3","writers":["src/gateway.js:21"],"removers":["src/gateway.js:34"],"note":"Gateway.sessions (container-field) pins Session, socket, decoder, recent buffer and the two socket listeners (gateway.js:24-25). Entry is removed only in release(), which runs only on the socket 'close' event. Server-initiated closes (bye, idle timeout, protocol error) in Session.close clear the heartbeat timer and destroy the socket but never call Gateway.release; with a socket whose destroy() does not emit 'close' (LoopbackSocket) the entry stays forever. Heartbeat timers are cleared correctly (node.timers=0), so the timer is not the holder. Missing pairing: sessions.delete on every close path. Repair class: remove-entry. Plain hang-up workload (load.js) plateaus, so it does not exercise this path. Caveat: trend did not tie heap_used to F3 by probe; growth tied via listeners at gateway.js:24/25 and heap_used slope ~3.4KB/session."}
